        "term": "Special Continuous Probability Distributions",
        "def": "Inversely use the standard Normal distribution table to determine the value of (i) standard normal random variable corresponding to a given value of the standard Normal cumulative distribution function, (ii) a normal random variable corresponding to a given value of a Normal cumulative distribution function and (iii) parameters of a normal random variable.\nAs you know that it is difficult to locate a specified value on a continuous random variable, that is why point probability in continuous case is always equal to zero and we compute probabilities for interval of values. In this unit we\nconsider only continuous uniform distribution and the Normal distribution. 4.1.1 Continuous uniform or rectangular probability distribution\nLike discrete case, continuous uniform distribution is the simplest probability distribution. It is used in the situations where the probability density"
